  <sharedProfiles>
    <profile name="Landing Boat Machine Gun" typeId="460e-d6f1-fb38-8723" typeName="Special Gear" hidden="false" id="e16e-492a-8545-59b2" publicationId="21ee-01ed-7eb0-72c8" page="5">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="a686-4c40-87a7-e7f2">If you have any Landing Boats deployed, once per Turn you may spend 2 Stars to fire one of their on-board Machine Guns, with the same stats as an Off-Table Machine Gun.  However, if an enemy model Shoots and &quot;Injures&quot; the Boat, or Moves onto it, the Boat&apos;s crew is captured and you lose access to its Machine Guns.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Landing Boat" typeId="9881-5d02-6f57-bc65" typeName="Squad Support" hidden="false" id="96d2-5993-0bb5-29d6" publicationId="21ee-01ed-7eb0-72c8" page="5">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="e807-c516-44d2-4199">Each Landing Boat replaces a Jump-Off.


Models can be assigned to a Landing Boat before the game begins.  Instead of using a Jump-Off, the first time a model assigned to a Landing Boat activated, they perform a Group Action in which the Boat is placed anywhere on your Squad&apos;s shoreline.  Once the Boat Lands, all the models assigned to it are placed anywhere within 9” of its front, provided it’s at least 6” away from the nearest enemy model or Jump-Off. That player may also decide to keep some or all of the models within the Boat, if they’d prefer.  See Pacific Heat, page 5.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
  </sharedProfiles>
  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Long Weapon" id="5e30-2087-9074-69f5" hidden="false" publicationId="21ee-01ed-7eb0-72c8" page="9">
      <description>Engages in Melee if they come within 2&quot; of an enemy, or an enemy comes within 2&quot; of them.  Subtracts 3D6 from opponents&apos; Melee Pool if they don&apos;t also have a Long Weapon.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Bren Steady" id="26d4-ac6b-92ee-5f6f" hidden="false" publicationId="21ee-01ed-7eb0-72c8" page="9">
      <description>This model may fire their Machine Gun as a Strike Weapon.</description>
      <comment>British</comment>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Jungle Fighter" id="9d03-ef66-c9a8-e7c9" hidden="false" publicationId="21ee-01ed-7eb0-72c8" page="9">
      <description>No penalty to Command Radius or Movement for being in a Jungle.  If it&apos;s a Dense Jungle, Movement penalty is -1&quot; per D6&quot;, rather than -2&quot;.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Scout" id="729a-3d54-3f72-0fd5" hidden="false" publicationId="21ee-01ed-7eb0-72c8" page="9">
      <comment>Pacific Version</comment>
      <description>May Appear within 9&quot; of a Jump-Off rather than 3&quot;.  If they use a Landing Boat, they may move up to 12&quot; when deploying, rather than 3&quot;.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ambush" id="0823-c466-4fc2-85d6" hidden="false" publicationId="21ee-01ed-7eb0-72c8" page="9">
      <description>When an Ambush model uses a Jump-Off inside a Jungle, they may appear up to 12&quot; away from it, rather than 3&quot;.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Standing Ready" id="f05c-838c-bd5e-d5ae" hidden="false" publicationId="af58-47f6-82b8-3f00" page="73">
      <description>May not Take Cover and cannot start of join a &quot;Hit the Deck!&quot; Group Action.  However, when determining starting Squad Morale, Squads led by this model roll twice and discard the lowest result.</description>
      <comment>British</comment>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
